{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029663-al-i-batin-and-the-changelings","id":1029663,"title":"Al I Batin and the Changelings?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-10T11:06:17-08:00","id":1029663,"title":"Al I Batin and the Changelings?","content":"So...im aware that the Al I Batin are heavy hitters when it comes to mind and subconcious mind... but what about dreams and changelings? how do they relate to them? whats their relationship","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:47:26-08:00","id":1029681,"title":"","content":"I don't think that they have a big relationship with them. They know a bit of the Eshu, that live in Africa. Both were allied to the Osirian League (mummy) back when Horus was young (not that many remember that).<br /> The Verbena and Dreamspeakers probably have more relationship with the fae in general than the Al I Batin.<br /> <br /> It must be noted that, while Mind has a lot to do with the dreams, it isn't the key Sphere when dealing with the Dreaming. Spirit it's the sphere that it's most realted to the Changelings as per old Changeling and Mage books. Dreamspeakers used to be able to &quot;step sideways&quot; to the Dreaming (instead of the Middle Umbra) using Spirit 3, as per the book of worlds. Since this was never mentioned again one can assume that this isn't supported in revised and beyond, but I think that Spirit should still be the main Sphere for stuff that has to do with the Dreaming (with Mind as a close second).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T17:36:10-08:00","id":1029838,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, while Batini were allied with mummies (and may have had contacts with the Eshu due that, possibly), this aliance wasn't early in the history of the mummies, as the Ahl-i-Batin appear in the Night of Fana, 514 BC.<br /> But the point was that nothing indicates any expertice in Changelings from this craft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T18:20:52-08:00","id":1029847,"title":"","content":"It's too bad CtD went under before their &quot;Year of Scarab&quot; release came out. I'd hope'd it was going to have had new Gallain for the Middle East (perhaps Djinn-themed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T18:39:07-08:00","id":1029855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029663-al-i-batin-and-the-changelings?p=1029847#post1029847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's too bad CtD went under before their &quot;Year of Scarab&quot; release came out. I'd hope'd it was going to have had new Gallain for the Middle East (perhaps Djinn-themed).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if they will ever publish &quot;WoD Location&quot; books which gives details on all things, from Vampires to Changelings. It could focus on a specific place/region like India for example, with each chapter specifically talking about the five main lines, detailing the local Kindred rule; the general Umbral battle field for the place (and local totems); Which tradition and crafts are milling about along with the Technocratic influence in place; Which Dark Kingdom looks over it, and some of the major citadels; and what the Dreaming looks like in the area.<br /> <br /> They already kinda did this with a Wraith book for Tokyo, a Changeling book for Britain, and a Vampire book for Mexico, but wouldn't it make more sense to have such books not be tied to a specific game line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T20:21:32-08:00","id":1029892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029663-al-i-batin-and-the-changelings?p=1029855#post1029855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wonder if they will ever publish &quot;WoD Location&quot; books which gives details on all things, from Vampires to Changelings. It could focus on a specific place/region like India for example, with each chapter specifically talking about the five main lines, detailing the local Kindred rule; the general Umbral battle field for the place (and local totems); Which tradition and crafts are milling about along with the Technocratic influence in place; Which Dark Kingdom looks over it, and some of the major citadels; and what the Dreaming looks like in the area.<br /> <br /> They already kinda did this with a Wraith book for Tokyo, a Changeling book for Britain, and a Vampire book for Mexico, but wouldn't it make more sense to have such books not be tied to a specific game line?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were the old <i>A World Of Darkness</i> books, but those were early White Wolf. We don't have an idea of what the whole setting looked like during the Revised era, let alone for the 20th anniversary.<br /> <br /> It would be nice to have a sort of WoD20 micro-line, updating some of the general setting material. You could have a new A World of Darkness book, a book about crossovers, and a book about playing normal, ordinary folks (I mean, we have a bit of that already with Hunters Hunted II, but it's not the same thing as having what Chronicles of Darkness has with its default, normal mortal rules). Maybe a translation guide for some of the books in CoD that didn't have full analogues in the cWoD, like Promethean or Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-12T05:12:47-08:00","id":1030522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1029663-al-i-batin-and-the-changelings?p=1029892#post1029892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were the old <i>A World Of Darkness</i> books, but those were early White Wolf. We don't have an idea of what the whole setting looked like during the Revised era, let alone for the 20th anniversary.<br /> <br /> It would be nice to have a sort of WoD20 micro-line, updating some of the general setting material. You could have a new A World of Darkness book, a book about crossovers, and a book about playing normal, ordinary folks (I mean, we have a bit of that already with Hunters Hunted II, but it's not the same thing as having what Chronicles of Darkness has with its default, normal mortal rules). Maybe a translation guide for some of the books in CoD that didn't have full analogues in the cWoD, like Promethean or Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While there wasn't a revised Era WOD book there was a 2e which I wouldn't call &quot;early&quot; <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}